# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in real values to run the Demo app. Then run
# `source scripts/load-env.sh` once per login session before building or opening Xcode — see
# scripts/load-env.sh for why a plain `export` isn't enough for a GUI-launched Xcode.

# The usp-widget "alfred" dev server the Demo mints orchestration sessions against.
# Run `npm run dev:alfred` from the usp-widget repo root, then point here.
# Leave blank to fall back to http://localhost:9001.
#
# Android's own .env says 10.0.2.2 — that is an *emulator* alias for the host loopback. The iOS
# Simulator shares the host's network stack, so localhost is correct here. A physical device needs
# your machine's LAN IP instead.
ALFRED_BASE_URL=
